{
  "name": "08-append-and-pins",
  "about": "Append prompts (injection_position 2) glued onto existing chat messages: user-role depth 0 (glues onto the current user turn, the last user-role message in the chat-history region), assistant-role depth 1 (glues one assistant message back), and a system-role append at depth 2 (system falls back to the user role per appendAtDepth, so it glues onto the second user message back). Four top pins and three bottom pins with distinct injection_order, each group declared out of injection_order sequence (D,B,A,C and B,C,A) so byte-identical output proves the port sorts by injection_order rather than trusting declaration/sort_order. Preset row carries explicit samplers (temperature/top_p/max_tokens) and an assistant_prefill in system_prompts. max_context is null on the preset row, a state a real ST import can never produce (openai_max_context defaults to 2000000 when absent), so this field is a deliberate hand-edit exercising preset-loader's null branch, not import-reproducible; assemblePrompt never reads presetPrompts.maxContext in this pin, so the field is inert and has no visible effect on conversationHistory here. A persona is attached (no extra prompt row) so the synthetic {{persona}} is visible between the top pins and the greeting. No relative/in-chat/chatHistory prompt is declared, so RoleCall's own auto-inject (lore/persona/summary/message_history) supplies the chat-history region the appends and pins need.",
